==Battleground==
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 10 seconds<sup>300f</sup>, delay 25.67~26.67 seconds<sup>770f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 11.33 seconds<sup>340f</sup>, delay 25.67~26.67 seconds<sup>770f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Gory Dark]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 25.67~26.67 seconds<sup>770f~800f</sup>.
*3 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 16.67~33.33 seconds<sup>500f~1,000f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Sir Rel]] (10%) spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 12~24 seconds<sup>360f~720f</sup>.
**8 [[Shadow Boxer K]]s spawn, delay 6~12 seconds<sup>180f~360f</sup>.
**12 [[Relic Doge]]s spawn, delay 4~16 seconds<sup>120f~480f</sup>.
**24 [[Sir Rel]]s (100%) spawn, delay 2~8 seconds<sup>60f~240f</sup>.
**2 [[Oldhorn]]s spawn, delay 50 seconds<sup>1,500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
[[Rodeo Cat]] with his Target Relic [[Talents|Talent]] works really well here, as the only traits present are ones he targets. Strong area attackers like [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Slapstick Cats]] or [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]] will be the core of your offense here. [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] can replace Rodeo if you don't have his Target Relic. Just make sure to stall some at the beginning to stack if possible.

